KG42.register("nodes-f5ec9db6bedc83b7c6efcbf7",{"id":"KG31-c38847500f58498d","code":"EXE010.1","label":"Execution of local electricity purchases and sales through an agent or operator","definition":"Under the source conditions, a local agent or operator, acting as the common purchase-and-sale counterparty, purchases participants' surplus electricity and sells electricity to electricity-purchasing participants; activation conditions, quantity rules, and the external-trading path after failure are retained source by source.","layer":"L7","template_code":"PGR","concept_id":"execution.energy_trade","concept_ids":["execution.energy_trade"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Execution object: electrical-energy purchase-and-sale of local participants","Counterparty relationship: a local agent or operator undertakes participants' selling and buying of electricity","Execution purpose: carry out the purchase-and-sale transactions in the local sharing arrangement","Execution boundary: participants and the local purchase-and-sale counterparty; external fallback serves only as a source-condition branch"]},"exclusions":[["After internal price coordination converges successfully within the iteration limit, prosumers agree to share, and the ESP purchases surplus electricity and sells it to other prosumers.","The success branch adopts a determined internal price set Pr; Algorithm 1 limits the number of iterations by K.","When the failure branch k>K is entered, prosumers may trade directly with the utility grid.","This unit uses Pr_buy for the ESP purchasing electricity from prosumers and Pr_sell for the ESP selling electricity to prosumers, retaining that price perspective."],["Executed in each time slot for PV prosumers n∈G; the unified counterparty is the MGO.","If E_n^g−x_n>0, the prosumer sells E_n^g−x_n to the MGO, and the established internal price p_s applies.","If E_n^g−x_n≤0, the prosumer purchases x_n−E_n^g from the MGO, and the established internal price p_b applies; the equality is retained, and the purchase quantity is zero when the net energy is zero.","The monetary-return formula only describes transaction receipts and expenditures and is not extended into a complete settlement definition."]],"members":[{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::V::execution.energy_trade","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Organizing energy-sharing exchanges requires a coordinator, instantiated as the Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Scope: Organization of PV energy sharing in the proposed energy-sharing zone. The ESP coordinates energy-sharing activities and executes the local trading agency role by purchasing surplus electricity from PV prosumers and selling electricity to other prosumers. Scope: ESP-mediated exchanges among PV prosumers in the energy-sharing zone. Internal unit prices apply to the ESP's electricity purchases from and sales to PV prosumers. Scope: The prosumer-facing legs of ESP purchases and sales within the energy-sharing zone. Local surplus-PV sharing is conditional on successful convergence of iterative price-signal coordination. In the successful branch the internal price is settled and prosumers agree to share; the failure branch leaves direct utility-grid trading available. Scope: Implementation of surplus-PV sharing through the distributed iterative process in Algorithm 1. Condition: The iterative internal-price coordination process converges to a fixed point within Algorithm 1's iteration limit; k > K is the stated failure branch.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"ESP-mediated exchanges among PV prosumers in the energy-sharing zone. | Implementation of surplus-PV sharing through the distributed iterative process in Algorithm 1. | Organization of PV energy sharing in the proposed energy-sharing zone. | The prosumer-facing legs of ESP purchases and sales within the energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-29"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"374605ad1b01a6db8884beca3c6b0faad6a333c662310321d595647cc6a10b0b","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003","node_id":"execution.energy_trade","function":"execution.energy_trade","unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::V::execution.energy_trade","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"The prosumer must sell its net surplus to the MGO, which purchases seller energy at the internal selling price p_s. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0 Under the source's nonpositive-net-energy branch, the prosumer must buy its net energy requirement from the MGO, which sells buyer energy at the internal buying price p_b. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"05b2d6278d5d838a1db5a0b90bc1ed3377894510310873b8482301f4cdbf854d","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005","node_id":"execution.energy_trade","function":"execution.energy_trade","unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::V::execution.energy_trade","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","market_meaning":"Selling surplus energy to the MGO produces prosumer revenue p_s(E_n^g − x_n). Scope: Stackelberg ESM: surplus-energy sales by a prosumer to the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0. A prosumer's energy purchase from the MGO has the monetary term p_b(E_n^g − x_n), represented as negative revenue in its utility. Scope: Stackelberg ESM: the buyer branch of prosumer transactions with the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Stackelberg ESM: surplus-energy sales by a prosumer to the MGO within the microgrid. | Stackelberg ESM: the buyer branch of prosumer transactions with the MGO within the microgrid.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C002"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"64b609dc3a061369f90c48874d70d705f1f6de16699e109c03b40e6e325458ca","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010","node_id":"execution.energy_trade","function":"execution.energy_trade","unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false}],"paper_ids":["06-sdr_energy_sharing","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"NSE FOR MICROGRIDS OF PEER-TO-PEER PROSUMERS 3571 In order to facilitate the organization of energy ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to facilitate the organization of energy sharing, a coordinator is required. Here, we introduce a new entity named Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Generally, the ESP may belong to the microgrid operator or an independent third party company that focuses on the business mode of energy sharing, which provides energy sharing service for all participated PV prosumers. The ESP acts as an agent for prosumers and is responsible for assuring the power balance and the payment balance in the energy sharing zone. In this regard, the ESP is in charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net power export, then selling electricity to other prosumers or the utility grid.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"In order to facilitate the organization of energy sharing, a coordinator is required. Here, we introduce a new entity named Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Generally, the ESP may belong to the microgrid operator or an independent third party company that focuses on the business mode of energy sharing, which provides energy sharing service for all participated PV prosumers. The ESP acts as an agent for prosumers and is responsible for assuring the power balance and the payment balance in the energy sharing zone. In this regard, the ESP is in charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net power export, then selling electricity to other prosumers or the utility grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e28","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":"3570","section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"ex- with price-based DR for microgrids of P2P prosumers. The main the contributions are as follows. ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"1) An energy sharing structure is proposed to integrate the autonomous PV prosumers into an energy sharing zone, and a virtual entity named energy sharing provider (ESP) is defined to coordinate the sharing activities. 2) A dynamical internal pricing model is proposed for the operation of energy sharing zone, which is defined based on the supply and demand ratio (SDR) of shared PV energy, and the feed-in tariff is considered as the price bound. 3) As the internal prices are adjusted with the change of SDR, the autonomous demand response of participants is integrated into the energy sharing, and the implementation method is also designed.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"1) An energy sharing structure is proposed to integrate the autonomous PV prosumers into an energy sharing zone, and a virtual entity named energy sharing provider (ESP) is defined to coordinate the sharing activities. 2) A dynamical internal pricing model is proposed for the operation of energy sharing zone, which is defined based on the supply and demand ratio (SDR) of shared PV energy, and the feed-in tariff is considered as the price bound. 3) As the internal prices are adjusted with the change of SDR, the autonomous demand response of participants is integrated into the energy sharing, and the implementation method is also designed."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"3572","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / B. Internal Price Model","anchor_text":"TSP h to SDRh = (7) TBP h th Considering the ﬂuctuation of PV power and users’ load, the λb SDR is a","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"As shown in Fig. 3, the ESP acts as an agent for all the PV prosumers. The ESP purchases power from PV prosumers and utility grid at the unit price of Pr_buy and \\lambda_{buy}, and sells power to PV prosumers and utility grid at the unit price of Pr_sell and \\lambda_{sell}, respectively.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"As shown in Fig. 3, the ESP acts as an agent for all the PV prosumers. The ESP purchases power from PV prosumers and utility grid at the unit price of Pr_buy and \\lambda_{buy}, and sells power to PV prosumers and utility grid at the unit price of Pr_sell and \\lambda_{sell}, respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-26","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-28","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"NSE FOR MICROGRIDS OF PEER-TO-PEER PROSUMERS 3575 Algorithm 1 Initialize T P i, P i, ,i = [1, 2, . .","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1\nInitialize \\mathbf{TP}_{i}, \\mathbf{P}_{i}, i = [1, 2, \\ldots, n]\nfor k = 1 to K do\n Collect NP_i from each U-EMS, randomly sample δ_{i,ω}^{h} of M realizations to generate NP_{i,ω_m};\n Calculate TSP and TBP: TSP_{ω_m}^{h} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i,ω_m}^{h}, NP_{i,ω_m}^{h} \u003c 0 ; TBP_{ω_m}^{h} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i,ω_m}^{h}, NP_{i,ω_m}^{h} ≥ 0\n Calculate SDR: SDR_{ω_m}^{h} = \\frac{TSP_{ω_m}^{h}}{TBP_{ω_m}^{h}}\n Central setting price: Pr_{ω_m}^{h} = f(SDR_{ω_m}^{h}),\n Local optimization at each U-EMS of PV prosumer:\n x_i = arg\\min_x \\frac{1}{M} \\sum_{m=1}^{M} \\sum_{h=1}^{H} \\left( Pr_{i,ω_m}^{h}\\left( x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}\\left( 1 + δ_{i,ω_m}^{h} \\right) \\right) + α_i · \\left( x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h} \\right)^{2} \\right)\n if \\left\\| Pr - Pr_{old} \\right\\| ≤ ε then stop iteration end if\nend for\nif k > K then The energy sharing model is unsolvable, and then PV prosumers trade with utility grid directly.\nelse The internal price is settled as Pr, PV prosumers agree to share the surplus PV energy in the microgrid.\nend if","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"Algorithm 1\nInitialize \\mathbf{TP}_{i}, \\mathbf{P}_{i}, i = [1, 2, \\ldots, n]\nfor k = 1 to K do\n Collect NP_i from each U-EMS, randomly sample δ_{i,ω}^{h} of M realizations to generate NP_{i,ω_m};\n Calculate TSP and TBP: TSP_{ω_m}^{h} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i,ω_m}^{h}, NP_{i,ω_m}^{h} \u003c 0 ; TBP_{ω_m}^{h} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i,ω_m}^{h}, NP_{i,ω_m}^{h} ≥ 0\n Calculate SDR: SDR_{ω_m}^{h} = \\frac{TSP_{ω_m}^{h}}{TBP_{ω_m}^{h}}\n Central setting price: Pr_{ω_m}^{h} = f(SDR_{ω_m}^{h}),\n Local optimization at each U-EMS of PV prosumer:\n x_i = arg\\min_x \\frac{1}{M} \\sum_{m=1}^{M} \\sum_{h=1}^{H} \\left( Pr_{i,ω_m}^{h}\\left( x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}\\left( 1 + δ_{i,ω_m}^{h} \\right) \\right) + α_i · \\left( x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h} \\right)^{2} \\right)\n if \\left\\| Pr - Pr_{old} \\right\\| ≤ ε then stop iteration end if\nend for\nif k > K then The energy sharing model is unsolvable, and then PV prosumers trade with utility grid directly.\nelse The internal price is settled as Pr, PV prosumers agree to share the surplus PV energy in the microgrid.\nend if"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-29","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 8. Load/power curves of the typical day in summer: (a) prosumers’ PV powe load curve and net po","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"If the iterative process converges to a ﬁxed point after a ﬁnite number of iterations, the energy sharing zone with internal price Pr converges and all PV prosumers can beneﬁt from this feasible solution. Otherwise, it is divergent, the energy sharing model is unsolvable and the PV prosumers still can trade with the utility grid directly.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"If the iterative process converges to a ﬁxed point after a ﬁnite number of iterations, the energy sharing zone with internal price Pr converges and all PV prosumers can beneﬁt from this feasible solution. Otherwise, it is divergent, the energy sharing model is unsolvable and the PV prosumers still can trade with the utility grid directly."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.B Profit Model of MGO","anchor_text":"( n n) ( ) act n∈B ave Es = (Egn −xn). (4) n∈S 0 In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosum","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"revenue of trading energy. In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for differ","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for different time slots, so we have extended the utility function as a piecewise function: U_n(x_n) = { k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_s(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_b(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (1) In (1), U_n(x_n) is the utility of prosumer n, k_n ln(1 + x_n) is the utility that the prosumer n achieves from consuming energy x_n. Note that k_n is the preference parameter of prosumer n, which changes with behavioral characteristics of the prosumer. It is shown in (1) that a prosumer with higher k_n would be more interested in consuming more x_n to attain its maximum utility level compared to a prosumer with lower preference. The ln(·) function has been widely used in economics for modeling the preference ordering of users and for decision making, and also recently been shown to be suitable for designing the utility for power consumers [23]. p_s(E_n^g − x_n) is the revenue that the prosumer receives from selling the rest of its energy, whereas p_b(E_n^g − x_n) is the negative revenue when the prosumer buys energy.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for different time slots, so we have extended the utility function as a piecewise function: U_n(x_n) = { k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_s(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_b(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (1) In (1), U_n(x_n) is the utility of prosumer n, k_n ln(1 + x_n) is the utility that the prosumer n achieves from consuming energy x_n. Note that k_n is the preference parameter of prosumer n, which changes with behavioral characteristics of the prosumer. It is shown in (1) that a prosumer with higher k_n would be more interested in consuming more x_n to attain its maximum utility level compared to a prosumer with lower preference. The ln(·) function has been widely used in economics for modeling the preference ordering of users and for decision making, and also recently been shown to be suitable for designing the utility for power consumers [23]. p_s(E_n^g − x_n) is the revenue that the prosumer receives from selling the rest of its energy, whereas p_b(E_n^g − x_n) is the negative revenue when the prosumer buys energy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","quote":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["convergence_conditioned_exchange_execution","net_energy_directional_exchange"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"KG31-L7-SC-L7-5c14067763c7f5c2","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L7","ontological_kind":"SC-L7-5c14067763c7f5c2"},"semantic_definition":{"definition":"Under the source conditions, a local agent or operator, acting as the common purchase-and-sale counterparty, purchases participants' surplus electricity and sells electricity to electricity-purchasing participants; activation conditions, quantity rules, and the external-trading path after failure are retained source by source.","identity_fields":["Execution object: electrical-energy purchase-and-sale of local participants","Counterparty relationship: a local agent or operator undertakes participants' selling and buying of electricity","Execution purpose: carry out the purchase-and-sale transactions in the local sharing arrangement","Execution boundary: participants and the local purchase-and-sale counterparty; external fallback serves only as a source-condition branch"]},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","paper_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"execution.energy_trade","source_occurrences":[{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::V::execution.energy_trade","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Organizing energy-sharing exchanges requires a coordinator, instantiated as the Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Scope: Organization of PV energy sharing in the proposed energy-sharing zone. The ESP coordinates energy-sharing activities and executes the local trading agency role by purchasing surplus electricity from PV prosumers and selling electricity to other prosumers. Scope: ESP-mediated exchanges among PV prosumers in the energy-sharing zone. Internal unit prices apply to the ESP's electricity purchases from and sales to PV prosumers. Scope: The prosumer-facing legs of ESP purchases and sales within the energy-sharing zone. Local surplus-PV sharing is conditional on successful convergence of iterative price-signal coordination. In the successful branch the internal price is settled and prosumers agree to share; the failure branch leaves direct utility-grid trading available. Scope: Implementation of surplus-PV sharing through the distributed iterative process in Algorithm 1. Condition: The iterative internal-price coordination process converges to a fixed point within Algorithm 1's iteration limit; k > K is the stated failure branch.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"ESP-mediated exchanges among PV prosumers in the energy-sharing zone. | Implementation of surplus-PV sharing through the distributed iterative process in Algorithm 1. | Organization of PV energy sharing in the proposed energy-sharing zone. | The prosumer-facing legs of ESP purchases and sales within the energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-29"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"374605ad1b01a6db8884beca3c6b0faad6a333c662310321d595647cc6a10b0b"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Organizing energy-sharing exchanges requires a coordinator, instantiated as the Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Scope: Organization of PV energy sharing in the proposed energy-sharing zone.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"NSE FOR MICROGRIDS OF PEER-TO-PEER PROSUMERS 3571 In order to facilitate the organization of energy ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to facilitate the organization of energy sharing, a coordinator is required. Here, we introduce a new entity named Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Generally, the ESP may belong to the microgrid operator or an independent third party company that focuses on the business mode of energy sharing, which provides energy sharing service for all participated PV prosumers. The ESP acts as an agent for prosumers and is responsible for assuring the power balance and the payment balance in the energy sharing zone. In this regard, the ESP is in charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net power export, then selling electricity to other prosumers or the utility grid."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The ESP coordinates energy-sharing activities and executes the local trading agency role by purchasing surplus electricity from PV prosumers and selling electricity to other prosumers. Scope: ESP-mediated exchanges among PV prosumers in the energy-sharing zone.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e28"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"NSE FOR MICROGRIDS OF PEER-TO-PEER PROSUMERS 3571 In order to facilitate the organization of energy ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to facilitate the organization of energy sharing, a coordinator is required. Here, we introduce a new entity named Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Generally, the ESP may belong to the microgrid operator or an independent third party company that focuses on the business mode of energy sharing, which provides energy sharing service for all participated PV prosumers. The ESP acts as an agent for prosumers and is responsible for assuring the power balance and the payment balance in the energy sharing zone. In this regard, the ESP is in charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net power export, then selling electricity to other prosumers or the utility grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e28","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":"3570","section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"ex- with price-based DR for microgrids of P2P prosumers. The main the contributions are as follows. ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"1) An energy sharing structure is proposed to integrate the autonomous PV prosumers into an energy sharing zone, and a virtual entity named energy sharing provider (ESP) is defined to coordinate the sharing activities. 2) A dynamical internal pricing model is proposed for the operation of energy sharing zone, which is defined based on the supply and demand ratio (SDR) of shared PV energy, and the feed-in tariff is considered as the price bound. 3) As the internal prices are adjusted with the change of SDR, the autonomous demand response of participants is integrated into the energy sharing, and the implementation method is also designed."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Internal unit prices apply to the ESP's electricity purchases from and sales to PV prosumers. Scope: The prosumer-facing legs of ESP purchases and sales within the energy-sharing zone.","expression":"Pr_buy = unit price for ESP purchases of electricity from PV prosumers; Pr_sell = unit price for ESP sales of electricity to PV prosumers","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-Pr_buy","v141-c-R003-Pr_sell"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"3572","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / B. Internal Price Model","anchor_text":"TSP h to SDRh = (7) TBP h th Considering the ﬂuctuation of PV power and users’ load, the λb SDR is a","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"As shown in Fig. 3, the ESP acts as an agent for all the PV prosumers. The ESP purchases power from PV prosumers and utility grid at the unit price of Pr_buy and \\lambda_{buy}, and sells power to PV prosumers and utility grid at the unit price of Pr_sell and \\lambda_{sell}, respectively."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C004","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Local surplus-PV sharing is conditional on successful convergence of iterative price-signal coordination. In the successful branch the internal price is settled and prosumers agree to share; the failure branch leaves direct utility-grid trading available. Scope: Implementation of surplus-PV sharing through the distributed iterative process in Algorithm 1. Condition: The iterative internal-price coordination process converges to a fixed point within Algorithm 1's iteration limit; k > K is the stated failure branch.","expression":"if k > K then unsolvable and PV prosumers trade with utility grid directly; else the internal price is settled as Pr and PV prosumers agree to share the surplus PV energy in the microgrid","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-K","v141-c-R003-Pr"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-29"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-26","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-28","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"NSE FOR MICROGRIDS OF PEER-TO-PEER PROSUMERS 3575 Algorithm 1 Initialize T P i, P i, ,i = [1, 2, . .","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1\nInitialize \\mathbf{TP}_{i}, \\mathbf{P}_{i}, i = [1, 2, \\ldots, n]\nfor k = 1 to K do\n Collect NP_i from each U-EMS, randomly sample δ_{i,ω}^{h} of M realizations to generate NP_{i,ω_m};\n Calculate TSP and TBP: TSP_{ω_m}^{h} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i,ω_m}^{h}, NP_{i,ω_m}^{h} \u003c 0 ; TBP_{ω_m}^{h} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i,ω_m}^{h}, NP_{i,ω_m}^{h} ≥ 0\n Calculate SDR: SDR_{ω_m}^{h} = \\frac{TSP_{ω_m}^{h}}{TBP_{ω_m}^{h}}\n Central setting price: Pr_{ω_m}^{h} = f(SDR_{ω_m}^{h}),\n Local optimization at each U-EMS of PV prosumer:\n x_i = arg\\min_x \\frac{1}{M} \\sum_{m=1}^{M} \\sum_{h=1}^{H} \\left( Pr_{i,ω_m}^{h}\\left( x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}\\left( 1 + δ_{i,ω_m}^{h} \\right) \\right) + α_i · \\left( x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h} \\right)^{2} \\right)\n if \\left\\| Pr - Pr_{old} \\right\\| ≤ ε then stop iteration end if\nend for\nif k > K then The energy sharing model is unsolvable, and then PV prosumers trade with utility grid directly.\nelse The internal price is settled as Pr, PV prosumers agree to share the surplus PV energy in the microgrid.\nend if"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-29","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 8. Load/power curves of the typical day in summer: (a) prosumers’ PV powe load curve and net po","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"If the iterative process converges to a ﬁxed point after a ﬁnite number of iterations, the energy sharing zone with internal price Pr converges and all PV prosumers can beneﬁt from this feasible solution. Otherwise, it is divergent, the energy sharing model is unsolvable and the PV prosumers still can trade with the utility grid directly."}]}],"variables":[],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-Pr_buy","symbol":"Pr_buy","meaning":"Internal buying price of the energy-sharing zone; unit price at which the ESP purchases electricity from PV prosumers on the prosumer-facing leg of energy-trade execution.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-Pr_buy"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-Pr_sell","symbol":"Pr_sell","meaning":"Internal selling price of the energy-sharing zone; unit price at which the ESP sells electricity to PV prosumers on the prosumer-facing leg of energy-trade execution.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-Pr_sell"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-K","symbol":"K","meaning":"Iteration limit of Algorithm 1 for the iterative internal-price coordination; k > K is the failure branch for energy-trade execution.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-28"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-K"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-Pr","symbol":"Pr","meaning":"Internal price set settled in the successful branch of Algorithm 1 after convergence; used for the prosumer-facing energy-sharing trades.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-29"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-Pr"}]},{"unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","paper_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"execution.energy_trade","source_occurrences":[{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::V::execution.energy_trade","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"The prosumer must sell its net surplus to the MGO, which purchases seller energy at the internal selling price p_s. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0 Under the source's nonpositive-net-energy branch, the prosumer must buy its net energy requirement from the MGO, which sells buyer energy at the internal buying price p_b. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"05b2d6278d5d838a1db5a0b90bc1ed3377894510310873b8482301f4cdbf854d"},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::V::execution.energy_trade","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","market_meaning":"Selling surplus energy to the MGO produces prosumer revenue p_s(E_n^g − x_n). Scope: Stackelberg ESM: surplus-energy sales by a prosumer to the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0. A prosumer's energy purchase from the MGO has the monetary term p_b(E_n^g − x_n), represented as negative revenue in its utility. Scope: Stackelberg ESM: the buyer branch of prosumer transactions with the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Stackelberg ESM: surplus-energy sales by a prosumer to the MGO within the microgrid. | Stackelberg ESM: the buyer branch of prosumer transactions with the MGO within the microgrid.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C002"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"64b609dc3a061369f90c48874d70d705f1f6de16699e109c03b40e6e325458ca"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The prosumer must sell its net surplus to the MGO, which purchases seller energy at the internal selling price p_s. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0","expression":"\\forall n\\in G:\\; E_n^g - x_n > 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\bigl(E_n^g - x_n \\text{ is sold to the MGO at } p_s\\bigr)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x-x_n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-theta-E_n^g","v141-c-R005-theta-p_s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.B Profit Model of MGO","anchor_text":"( n n) ( ) act n∈B ave Es = (Egn −xn). (4) n∈S 0 In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosum","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Under the source's nonpositive-net-energy branch, the prosumer must buy its net energy requirement from the MGO, which sells buyer energy at the internal buying price p_b. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0","expression":"\\forall n\\in G:\\; E_n^g - x_n \\le 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\bigl(x_n - E_n^g \\text{ is bought from the MGO at } p_b\\bigr)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x-x_n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-theta-E_n^g","v141-c-R005-theta-p_b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.B Profit Model of MGO","anchor_text":"( n n) ( ) act n∈B ave Es = (Egn −xn). (4) n∈S 0 In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosum","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Selling surplus energy to the MGO produces prosumer revenue p_s(E_n^g − x_n). Scope: Stackelberg ESM: surplus-energy sales by a prosumer to the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0.","expression":"p_s (E_n^g - x_n)  for  E_n^g - x_n > 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R010-x-n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R010-ps","v141-c-R010-Eng"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"revenue of trading energy. In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for differ","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for different time slots, so we have extended the utility function as a piecewise function: U_n(x_n) = { k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_s(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_b(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (1) In (1), U_n(x_n) is the utility of prosumer n, k_n ln(1 + x_n) is the utility that the prosumer n achieves from consuming energy x_n. Note that k_n is the preference parameter of prosumer n, which changes with behavioral characteristics of the prosumer. It is shown in (1) that a prosumer with higher k_n would be more interested in consuming more x_n to attain its maximum utility level compared to a prosumer with lower preference. The ln(·) function has been widely used in economics for modeling the preference ordering of users and for decision making, and also recently been shown to be suitable for designing the utility for power consumers [23]. p_s(E_n^g − x_n) is the revenue that the prosumer receives from selling the rest of its energy, whereas p_b(E_n^g − x_n) is the negative revenue when the prosumer buys energy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"A prosumer's energy purchase from the MGO has the monetary term p_b(E_n^g − x_n), represented as negative revenue in its utility. Scope: Stackelberg ESM: the buyer branch of prosumer transactions with the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0.","expression":"p_b (E_n^g - x_n)  for  E_n^g - x_n \u003c= 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R010-x-n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R010-pb","v141-c-R010-Eng"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"revenue of trading energy. In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for differ","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for different time slots, so we have extended the utility function as a piecewise function: U_n(x_n) = { k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_s(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_b(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (1) In (1), U_n(x_n) is the utility of prosumer n, k_n ln(1 + x_n) is the utility that the prosumer n achieves from consuming energy x_n. Note that k_n is the preference parameter of prosumer n, which changes with behavioral characteristics of the prosumer. It is shown in (1) that a prosumer with higher k_n would be more interested in consuming more x_n to attain its maximum utility level compared to a prosumer with lower preference. The ln(·) function has been widely used in economics for modeling the preference ordering of users and for decision making, and also recently been shown to be suitable for designing the utility for power consumers [23]. p_s(E_n^g − x_n) is the revenue that the prosumer receives from selling the rest of its energy, whereas p_b(E_n^g − x_n) is the negative revenue when the prosumer buys energy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R005-x-x_n","symbol":"x_n","meaning":"Energy consumed by prosumer n in one time slot; it determines the prosumer's net trade E_n^g - x_n with the MGO.","kind":"operational","domain":"n ∈ G (set of PV prosumers); prosumer energy consumption in one time slot; no explicit numeric bounds are stated in the supplied R005 evidence","unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-x_n"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R010-x-n","symbol":"x_n","meaning":"Energy consumed by prosumer n in a time slot; the source defines the traded net energy as E_n^g - x_n. In this payment rule it is the consumption quantity entering the settlement term.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy consumption values for prosumer n in a time slot; numeric bounds are not specified by this rule's attached evidence.","unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x-n"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-theta-E_n^g","symbol":"E_n^g","meaning":"Energy produced by prosumer n in the same time slot; input to the net trade E_n^g - x_n.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-E_n^g"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-theta-p_s","symbol":"p_s","meaning":"Internal selling price at which the MGO purchases seller energy in this execution branch; treated as an input price for this activation-stage rule.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e014"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-p_s"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-theta-p_b","symbol":"p_b","meaning":"Internal buying price at which the MGO sells buyer energy in this execution branch; treated as an input price for this activation-stage rule.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e014"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-p_b"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R010-ps","symbol":"p_s","meaning":"Internal selling price set by the MGO, used for seller revenue in the surplus branch E_n^g - x_n > 0.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-ps"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R010-pb","symbol":"p_b","meaning":"Internal buying price set by the MGO, used for the buyer negative-revenue term in the nonpositive-net branch E_n^g - x_n \u003c= 0.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-pb"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R010-Eng","symbol":"E_n^g","meaning":"Energy produced by prosumer n in the relevant time slot; it enters the net traded energy E_n^g - x_n used by the payment term.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R010","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-Eng"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","stage":"L7","subtype":"convergence_conditioned_exchange_execution","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"After internal price coordination converges successfully within the iteration limit, prosumers agree to share, and the ESP purchases surplus electricity and sells it to other prosumers; if the failure branch k>K is entered, prosumers may trade directly with the utility grid.","form_kind":"procedural","identity_fields":["Object: local surplus-electricity sharing transactions","Core operation: according to the coordination result, activate agent purchase-and-sale or enter the external-trading fallback branch","Output: execute sharing or retain the direct grid-trading path"],"variation_fields":["The ESP assumes the role of purchase-and-sale agent","The success branch adopts a determined internal price set Pr","Algorithm 1 limits the number of iterations by K","This unit's transaction-side wording uses Pr_buy for the ESP purchasing electricity from prosumers and Pr_sell for the ESP selling electricity to prosumers"],"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004"],"paper_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"execution.energy_trade","template_code":"PGR"},{"unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","stage":"L7","subtype":"net_energy_directional_exchange","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"In each time slot, if E_n^g−x_n>0, the prosumer sells E_n^g−x_n to the MGO and p_s applies; if E_n^g−x_n≤0, the prosumer purchases x_n−E_n^g from the MGO and p_b applies.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: net electrical-energy exchange between participants and the operator","Core operation: execute a sale or a purchase according to the sign of the net energy","Output: transaction direction, counterparty, and exchange quantity"],"variation_fields":["The participants are PV prosumers n∈G, and the unified counterparty is the MGO","Executed time slot by time slot; p_s and p_b are established internal prices","The equality in the non-positive branch is retained; when the net energy is zero, the transaction quantity of that branch is zero","The monetary-return formula describes transaction receipts and expenditures and is not extended into a complete settlement definition of this node"],"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::v141-c-R010-C002"],"paper_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"execution.energy_trade","template_code":"PGR"}],"source_variants":[{"unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","retained_variants":["After internal price coordination converges successfully within the iteration limit, prosumers agree to share, and the ESP purchases surplus electricity and sells it to other prosumers.","The success branch adopts a determined internal price set Pr; Algorithm 1 limits the number of iterations by K.","When the failure branch k>K is entered, prosumers may trade directly with the utility grid.","This unit uses Pr_buy for the ESP purchasing electricity from prosumers and Pr_sell for the ESP selling electricity to prosumers, retaining that price perspective."],"evidence_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade::projection"]},{"unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","retained_variants":["Executed in each time slot for PV prosumers n∈G; the unified counterparty is the MGO.","If E_n^g−x_n>0, the prosumer sells E_n^g−x_n to the MGO, and the established internal price p_s applies.","If E_n^g−x_n≤0, the prosumer purchases x_n−E_n^g from the MGO, and the established internal price p_b applies; the equality is retained, and the purchase quantity is zero when the net energy is zero.","The monetary-return formula only describes transaction receipts and expenditures and is not extended into a complete settlement definition."],"evidence_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade::projection"]}],"functional":{"is_child":true,"subdivision_pending":false,"baseline_parent_id":"COMP-45cd67e262bf2b5f","baseline_parent_code":"EXE010","secondary_class":"SC-L7-5c14067763c7f5c2","category":{"id":"SC-L7-5c14067763c7f5c2","stage":"L7","label_zh":"Local electrical-energy purchase-and-sale undertaken by the operator","definition_zh":"In a local sharing arrangement, an agent or operator that bears the purchase-and-sale function acts as the participants' common counterparty and carries out purchase of surplus electricity and sale of electricity to demand; activation, direction determination, and exit paths are retained by source.","main_identity_axes":["Implementation obligation: carry out local electrical-energy purchase-and-sale","Counterparty relationship: participants and the local purchase-and-sale agent or operator","Activation purpose: execute local sharing transactions","Operational boundary: local participant—operator transaction relationship"],"inclusion_criteria":["It is specified that a local agent or operator undertakes participants' selling and buying of electricity.","The primary execution content is local electrical-energy purchase-and-sale; a convergence condition, a direction rule, or external fallback may serve as a source branch within an atomic unit."],"exclusion_criteria":["The primary function is external balancing of regionally aggregated surplus and shortage, or price-spread-driven cross-market resale.","Only an organizer identity is present, without its role as a purchase-and-sale counterparty being expressed.","The primary function is direct physical delivery among peers, automatic trading of virtual accounts, fund coverage, or a generating-unit control interface."],"supporting_unit_ids":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade"],"status":"agent_defined_structurally_validated"},"definition":{"definition_zh":"Under the source conditions, a local agent or operator, acting as the common purchase-and-sale counterparty, purchases participants' surplus electricity and sells electricity to electricity-purchasing participants; activation conditions, quantity rules, and the external-trading path after failure are retained source by source.","identity_fields":["Execution object: electrical-energy purchase-and-sale of local participants","Counterparty relationship: a local agent or operator undertakes participants' selling and buying of electricity","Execution purpose: carry out the purchase-and-sale transactions in the local sharing arrangement","Execution boundary: participants and the local purchase-and-sale counterparty; external fallback serves only as a source-condition branch"],"member_unit_ids":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade"]}},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/329"});
